" (https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0913/2026091300025.pdf)\nciteturn774view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 31; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn773view0\",\"id\":18}); Total lines: 1044\nL0@P0: – 1 –\nL1@P0: Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing Limited and The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong Limited\nL2@P0: take no responsibility for the contents of this announcement, make no representation as to\nL3@P0: its accuracy or completeness and expressly disclaim any liability whatsoever for any loss\nL4@P0: howsoever arising from or in reliance upon the whole or any part of the contents of this\nL5@P0: announcement.\nL6@P0: This announcement is for information purposes only and does not constitute an invitation\nL7@P0: or solicitation of an offer to acquire, purchase or subscribe for securities or an invitation\nL8@P0: to enter into an agreement to do any such things, nor is it calculated to invite any offer to\nL9@P0: acquire, purchase or subscribe for any securities.\nL10@P0: Neither this announcement nor any copy thereof may be released into or distributed directly\nL11@P0: or indirectly in the United States or any other jurisdiction where such release or distribution\nL12@P0: might be unlawful. This announcement does not constitute or form a part of any offer or\nL13@P0: solicitation to purchase or subscribe for securities in the United States. The securities\nL14@P0: mentioned herein have not been, and will not be, registered under the U.S. Securities Act, and\nL15@P0: may not be offered or sold in the United States unless registered under the U.S. Securities Act\nL16@P0: or pursuant to an exemption from, or in a transaction not subject to, registration under the\nL17@P0: U.S. Securities Act. The Company’s shares mentioned herein are being offered and sold (i) in\nL18@P0: the United States solely to qualified institutional buyers in reliance on Rule 144A or another\nL19@P0: exemption from the registration requirements of the U.S. Securities Act, and (ii) outside\nL20@P0: the United States in offshore transactions in accordance with Regulation S under the U.S.\nL21@P0: Securities Act. The Company has no intention to register under the U.S. Securities Act any\nL22@P0: of the securities referred to herein or to conduct a public offering of securities in the United\nL23@P0: States.\nL24@P0: Z.AI Co., Ltd.\nL25@P0: 北京智譜華章科技股份有限公司\nL26@P0: (A joint stock company established in the People’s Republic of China with limited liability)\nL27@P0: (Stock Code: 2513)\nL28@P0: (1) PLACING OF NEW H SHARES UNDER GENERAL MANDATE;\nL29@P0: AND\nL30@P0: (2) CONCURRENT PROPOSED ISSUE OF\nL31@P0: RMB20.14 BILLION U.S. DOLLAR SETTLED ZERO COUPON\nL32@P0: CONVERTIBLE BONDS DUE 2027 UNDER GENERAL MANDATE\nL33@P0: Sole Global Coordinator, Joint Bookrunner and Joint Lead Manager\nL34@P0-1: Joint Bookrunner and Joint Lead Manager– 2 –\nL35@P1: PLACING OF NEW H SHARES UNDER GENERAL MANDATE\nL36@P1: The Board is pleased to announce that on September 12, 2026, the Company and the Joint\nL37@P1: Placing Agents entered into the Placing Agreement, pursuant to which the Company agrees\nL38@P1: to appoint the Joint Placing Agents, and the Joint Placing Agents have agreed to act as the\nL39@P1: agents of the Company, to procure not less than six (6) Placees, who will be professional,\nL40@P1: institutional or other investors, and who and whose ultimate beneficial owners shall be the\nL41@P1: Independent Third Parties, on a best effort basis, to subscribe for up to 21,965,000 new H\nL42@P1: Shares at the Placing Price of HK$714.00 per Placing Share.\nL43@P1: It is expected that none of the Placees will become a substantial shareholder of the Company\nL44@P1: immediately after the completion of the Placing. To the best of the Directors’ knowledge,\nL45@P1: information and belief, having made all reasonable enquiries, each of the Joint Placing\nL46@P1: Agents and their respective ultimate beneficial owners are Independent Third Parties.\nL47@P1: The total number of Placing Shares under the Placing is up to 21,965,000 new H Shares,\nL48@P1: representing approximately 4.72% of the number of Shares in issue (i.e. 465,623,090\nL49@P1: Shares) as at the date of this announcement and approximately 4.50% of the number of\nL50@P1: Shares in issue as enlarged by the allotment and issuance of the Placing Shares (assuming\nL51@P1: that the Placing Shares are fully placed and except for the Placing Shares allotted and issued,\nL52@P1: there is no change in the issued Shares from the date of this announcement up to the date\nL53@P1: of completion of the Placing). The Company had no Treasury Shares as of the date of this\nL54@P1: announcement.\nL55@P1: The Placing Price of HK$714.00 per Placing Share represents: (a) a discount of\nL56@P1: approximately 9.96% to the closing price of HK$793.00 per H Share as quoted on the Stock\nL57@P1: Exchange on September 11, 2026 (being the trading day immediately prior to the date on\nL58@P1: which the Placing Agreement was signed); and (b) a discount of approximately 19.95% to\nL59@P1: the average closing price of approximately HK$891.90 per H Share as quoted on the Stock\nL60@P1: Exchange for the last five consecutive trading days up to and including September 11, 2026,\nL61@P1: being the trading day immediately prior to the date on which the Placing Agreement was\nL62@P1: signed.\nL63@P1: Assuming that the total number of Placing Shares is placed to the Placees in full, the\nL64@P1: total gross proceeds from the Placing are expected to be approximately HK$15,683.01\nL65@P1: million, and the net proceeds (after deducting commission and estimated expenses) from\nL66@P1: the Placing are expected to be approximately HK$15,664.13 million in aggregate. The net\nL67@P1: proceeds from the Placing will be used in the manner detailed in the section headed “Use of\nL68@P1-2: Proceeds” below. – 3 –\nL69@P2: The Placing Shares will be issued by the Company under the General Mandate, pursuant to\nL70@P2: which the Board is authorized to allot, issue and deal with up to 89,168,618 Shares (including\nL71@P2: securities convertible into such Shares), equivalent to 20% of the 445,843,090 Shares in issue\nL72@P2: as at the date of the annual general meeting of the Company held on June 22, 2026. As at\nL73@P2: the date of this announcement, 19,780,000 Shares have been allotted and issued under the\nL74@P2: General Mandate pursuant to the First Placing (as defined below). The placing and issue of\nL75@P2: the Placing Shares is not subject to the Shareholders’ further approval.\nL76@P2: The Company will apply to the Listing Committee for listing of, and permission to deal in,\nL77@P2: the Placing Shares.\nL78@P2: As the completion of the Placing is subject to the fulfilment of certain conditions\nL79@P2: precedent and the Joint Placing Agents not exercising their termination right, the\nL80@P2: Placing may or may not proceed. Shareholders and potential investors of the Company\nL81@P2: are advised to exercise caution when dealing in the securities of the Company.\nL82@P2: CONCURRENT PROPOSED ISSUE OF THE BONDS UNDER GENERAL\nL83@P2: MANDATE\nL84@P2: The Board is pleased to announce that on September 12, 2026, the Company and the\nL85@P2: Managers entered into the Subscription Agreement, pursuant to which and subject to\nL86@P2: certain conditions contained therein, the Company has agreed to issue, and the Managers\nL87@P2: have agreed to, severally and not jointly, subscribe and pay for, or procure subscribers to\nL88@P2: subscribe and pay for, the Bonds in an aggregate principal amount of RMB20.14 billion.\nL89@P2: The Placing and the issue of the Bonds are independent of each other and are not inter\u0002conditional.\nL90@P2: A book-building exercise has been conducted by the Managers, after which the terms of the\nL91@P2: Bonds, including but not limited to, the principal amount and the initial Conversion Price,\nL92@P2: have been determined.\nL93@P2: The Bonds are convertible in the circumstances set out in the Terms and Conditions into\nL94@P2: new H Shares at an initial Conversion Price of HK$892.50 per Conversion Share (subject to\nL95@P2-3: adjustments).– 4 –\nL96@P3: The initial Conversion Price is HK$892.50 per Conversion Share, which represents: (a) a\nL97@P3: premium of approximately 12.55% over the closing price of HK$793.00 per H Share as\nL98@P3: quoted on the Stock Exchange on September 11, 2026 (being the trading day immediately\nL99@P3: prior to the date on which the Subscription Agreement was signed); and (b) a premium of\nL100@P3: approximately 0.07% over the average closing price of approximately HK$891.90 per H\nL101@P3: Share as quoted on the Stock Exchange for the last five consecutive trading days up to and\nL102@P3: including September 11, 2026, being the trading day immediately prior to the date on which\nL103@P3: the Subscription Agreement was signed.\nL104@P3: Assuming full conversion of the Bonds at the initial Conversion Price, the Bonds will be\nL105@P3: convertible into approximately 26,365,026 Conversion Shares, representing approximately\nL106@P3: 5.66% of the number of Shares in issue as at the date of this announcement and approximately\nL107@P3: 5.36% of the number of Shares in issue as enlarged by the issue of the Conversion Shares\nL108@P3: upon the full conversion of the Bonds. The Conversion Shares will be fully-paid and rank\nL109@P3: pari passu in all respects with the H Shares then in issue on the relevant registration date,\nL110@P3: except for any right excluded by mandatory provisions of applicable law.\nL111@P3: Subject to completion of the Subscription, the total gross proceeds from the issue of the\nL112@P3: Bonds are expected to be approximately US$3,015.64 million (equivalent to approximately\nL113@P3: HK$23,648.44 million), and the net proceeds (after deducting the Managers’ commissions\nL114@P3: and other estimated expenses) from the issue of the Bonds are expected to be approximately\nL115@P3: US$3,010.77 million (equivalent to approximately HK$23,610.24 million), representing\nL116@P3: a net issue price of approximately HK$895.51 per Conversion Share based on the initial\nL117@P3: Conversion Price (subject to adjustments). The net proceeds will be used in the manner\nL118@P3: detailed in the section headed “Use of Proceeds” below.\nL119@P3: The Conversion Shares will be allotted and issued by the Company pursuant to the General\nL120@P3: Mandate, and the issue of the Bonds and the allotment and issue of the Conversion Shares\nL121@P3: are not subject to the Shareholders’ further approval.\nL122@P3: The Company will apply to the Vienna MTF operated by the Vienna Stock Exchange for the\nL123@P3: listing of the Bonds. The Company will also apply to the Listing Committee for the listing\nL124@P3: of, and permission to deal in, the Conversion Shares to be issued upon conversion of the\nL125@P3: Bonds.\nL126@P3: As completion of the Subscription is subject to the satisfaction of certain conditions\nL127@P3: precedent and the termination rights of the Managers, the Bonds may or may not be\nL128@P3: issued and/or the Conversion Shares may or may not be issued or listed. Shareholders\nL129@P3: and potential investors of the Company are advised to exercise caution when dealing in\nL130@P3-4: the securities of the Company.– 5 –\nL131@P4: PLACING OF NEW H SHARES UNDER GENERAL MANDATE\nL132@P4: The Board is pleased to announce that on September 12, 2026, the Company and the Joint\nL133@P4: Placing Agents entered into the Placing Agreement, pursuant to which the Company agrees\nL134@P4: to appoint the Joint Placing Agents, and the Joint Placing Agents have agreed to act as the\nL135@P4: agents of the Company, to procure not less than six (6) Placees, who will be professional,\nL136@P4: institutional or other investors, and who and whose ultimate beneficial owners shall be the\nL137@P4: Independent Third Parties, on a best effort basis, to subscribe for up to 21,965,000 new H\nL138@P4: Shares at the Placing Price of HK$714.00 per Placing Share.\nL139@P4: The principal terms of the Placing Agreement are as follows:\nL140@P4: Placing Agreement\nL141@P4: Date\nL142@P4: September 12, 2026\nL143@P4: Parties\nL144@P4: (1) The Company; and\nL145@P4: (2) The Joint Placing Agents.\nL146@P4: To the best of the Directors’ knowledge, information and belief, having made all reasonable\nL147@P4: enquiries, each of the Joint Placing Agents and their respective ultimate beneficial owner(s)\nL148@P4: are Independent Third Parties.\nL149@P4: Placees\nL150@P4: It is expected that the Joint Placing Agents will procure not less than six (6) Placees, who\nL151@P4: will be professional, institutional or other investors, on a best effort basis, to subscribe for the\nL152@P4: Placing Shares.\nL153@P4: The Placees of the Placing Shares shall be determined by the Joint Placing Agents subject\nL154@P4: to the requirements of the Listing Rules, and each of the Placees and its ultimate beneficial\nL155@P4: owners shall be Independent Third Parties. It is expected that none of the Placees will become\nL156@P4-5: a substantial shareholder of the Company immediately after the completion of the Placing. – 6 –\nL157@P5: Placing Shares\nL158@P5: The total number of Placing Shares under the Placing is up to 21,965,000 new H Shares,\nL159@P5: representing approximately 4.72% of the 465,623,090 Shares in issue as at the date of this\nL160@P5: announcement and approximately 4.50% of the Shares in issue as enlarged by the allotment\nL161@P5: and issuance of the Placing Shares (assuming that the Placing Shares are fully placed and\nL162@P5: except for the Placing Shares allotted and issued, there is no change in the issued Shares of the\nL163@P5: Company from the date of this announcement up to the date of completion of the Placing).\nL164@P5: Placing Price\nL165@P5: The Placing Price of HK$714.00 per Placing Share represents:\nL166@P5: (a) a discount of approximately 9.96% to the closing price of HK$793.00 per H Share\nL167@P5: as quoted on the Stock Exchange on September 11, 2026 (being the trading day\nL168@P5: immediately prior to the date on which the Placing Agreement was signed); and\nL169@P5: (b) a discount of approximately 19.95% to the average closing price of approximately\nL170@P5: HK$891.90 per H Share as quoted on the Stock Exchange for the last five consecutive\nL171@P5: trading days up to and including September 11, 2026, being the trading day immediately\nL172@P5: prior to the date on which the Placing Agreement was signed.\nL173@P5: The Placing Price was determined based on the market conditions and the prevailing market\nL174@P5: prices of the Shares and was arrived at by the Company and the Joint Placing Agents through\nL175@P5: arm’s length negotiation.\nL176@P5: Placing Commission\nL177@P5: The placing commission payable to the Joint Placing Agents under the Placing Agreement was\nL178@P5: arrived at after arm’s length negotiations between the Company and the Joint Placing Agents\nL179@P5: with reference to the prevailing market commission rate for similar transactions.\nL180@P5: Rights of the Placing Shares\nL181@P5: The Placing Shares will be allotted and issued by the Company under the General Mandate\nL182@P5: and, when allotted and issued by the Company, shall rank pari passu in all respects with\nL183@P5: other Shares in issue at that time, which are free from all liens, charges and encumbrances,\nL184@P5: and together with all rights attaching thereto as at the issuance date of the Placing Shares,\nL185@P5: including the right to receive all dividends declared, made or paid on or after the date of issue\nL186@P5-6: of the Placing Shares.– 7 –\nL187@P6: Conditions of the Placing\nL188@P6: Completion of the Placing is conditional upon the satisfaction or waiver (if applicable) of the\nL189@P6: following conditions, among others:\nL190@P6: (a) the Listing Committee of the Stock Exchange granting the listing of, and permission to\nL191@P6: deal in, the Placing Shares (and such listing and permission not subsequently revoked\nL192@P6: prior to the Completion); and\nL193@P6: (b) the Joint Placing Agents having received on the Closing Date (as defined below) the\nL194@P6: relevant legal opinions and other documentation as set out in the Placing Agreement.\nL195@P6: Save for condition (a) above, the Joint Placing Agents shall have the sole discretion to waive\nL196@P6: the other conditions for the Placing as set out above.\nL197@P6: Completion of the Placing\nL198@P6: Subject to the satisfaction or waiver of the conditions of the Placing, the completion of the\nL199@P6: Placing shall take place on September 16, 2026 or such other time and/or date as the Company\nL200@P6: and the Joint Placing Agents agree in writing (the “Closing Date”).\nL201@P6: Application for Listing\nL202@P6: The Company will apply to the Listing Committee for listing of, and permission to deal in, the\nL203@P6: Placing Shares.\nL204@P6: Filing with Regulatory Authorities in the PRC\nL205@P6: The Company will comply with the CSRC Rules and complete the CSRC Filing in connection\nL206@P6: with the Placing in accordance with the applicable requirements under the CSRC Filing Rules.\nL207@P6: Lock-up Undertakings by the Company under the Placing Agreement\nL208@P6: The Company has undertaken to the Joint Placing Agents in the Placing Agreement that the\nL209@P6: Company shall not, without the prior written consent of the Joint Placing Agents, (i) effect or\nL210@P6: arrange or procure placement of, allot or issue or offer to allot or issue or grant any option,\nL211@P6: right or warrant to subscribe for, or enter into any transaction which is designed to, or might\nL212@P6: reasonably be expected to, result in any of the aforesaid (whether by actual disposition or\nL213@P6: effective economic disposition due to cash settlement or otherwise), directly or indirectly,\nL214@P6: any equity securities of the Company or any securities convertible into, or exercisable, or\nL215@P6: exchangeable for, equity securities of the Company, or (ii) enter into any swap or similar\nL216@P6-7: agreement that transfers, in whole or in part, the economic risk of ownership of such Shares, – 8 –\nL217@P7: whether any such transaction described in (i) or (ii) above is to be settled by delivery of\nL218@P7: Shares or such other securities, in cash or otherwise, or (iii) publicly announce an intention to\nL219@P7: effect any such transaction, for a period beginning on the date of the Placing Agreement and\nL220@P7: ending on the date which is 60 days after the Closing Date. The foregoing shall not apply to\nL221@P7: (a) the issue of the Placing Shares, (b) the issue of the Bonds and the issue of any H Shares\nL222@P7: pursuant to the exercise of the conversion rights attaching to the Bonds, and (c) the allotment\nL223@P7: and issuance of any Shares or the grant of equity-based awards pursuant to the terms of\nL224@P7: 2026 share award scheme of the Company adopted on June 22, 2026 in compliance with the\nL225@P7: applicable requirements of the Listing Rules from time to time.\nL226@P7: As the completion of the Placing is subject to the fulfilment of certain conditions\nL227@P7: precedent and the Joint Placing Agents not exercising their termination right, the\nL228@P7: Placing may or may not proceed. Shareholders and potential investors of the Company\nL229@P7: are advised to exercise caution when dealing in the securities of the Company.\nL230@P7: CONCURRENT PROPOSED ISSUE OF THE BONDS UNDER GENERAL MANDATE\nL231@P7: The Board is pleased to announce that on September 12, 2026, the Company and the Managers\nL232@P7: entered into the Subscription Agreement, pursuant to which and subject to certain conditions\nL233@P7: contained therein, the Company has agreed to issue, and the Managers have agreed to,\nL234@P7: severally and not jointly, subscribe and pay for, or procure subscribers to subscribe and pay\nL235@P7: for, the Bonds in an aggregate principal amount of RMB20.14 billion.\nL236@P7: The principal terms of the Subscription Agreement are set out below.\nL237@P7: The Subscription Agreement\nL238@P7: Date\nL239@P7: September 12, 2026\nL240@P7: Parties\nL241@P7: (1) The Company as issuer; and\nL242@P7-8: (2) The Managers.– 9 –\nL243@P8: Subscription\nL244@P8: Subject to the satisfaction of the conditions set out below under “Conditions of the\nL245@P8: Subscription”, the Managers have agreed to, severally and not jointly, subscribe and pay for,\nL246@P8: or procure subscribers to subscribe and pay for, the Bonds in an aggregate principal amount\nL247@P8: of RMB20.14 billion. The Placing and the issue of the Bonds are independent of each other\nL248@P8: and are not inter-conditional. To the best of the Directors’ knowledge, information and belief,\nL249@P8: having made all reasonable enquiries, each of the Managers is an Independent Third Party.\nL250@P8: Subscribers\nL251@P8: The Managers have informed the Company that the Bonds will be offered to not less than six\nL252@P8: (6) independent subscribers, who will be independent individual, corporate and/or institutional\nL253@P8: professional investors. To the best of the Directors’ knowledge, information and belief, having\nL254@P8: made all reasonable enquiries, each of the subscribers and their respective ultimate beneficial\nL255@P8: owners is or will be an Independent Third Party.\nL256@P8: Conditions of the Subscription\nL257@P8: Completion of the Subscription is conditional upon the satisfaction or waiver (if applicable) of\nL258@P8: the following conditions, among others:\nL259@P8: (a) the Managers being satisfied with the results of their due diligence investigations with\nL260@P8: respect to the Company and its subsidiaries;\nL261@P8: (b) the Managers having received legal opinions, each dated the Issue Date and in a form\nL262@P8: reasonably acceptable to the Managers jointly, of legal advisers to the Company as to\nL263@P8: Hong Kong law and English law, of legal advisers to the Company as to PRC law, and of\nL264@P8: legal advisers to the Managers as to PRC law;\nL265@P8: (c) the Managers having received such legal opinions, certificates (including incumbency\nL266@P8: certificates), constitutive documents, Board resolutions, corporate approvals and\nL267@P8: authorisations or consents in relation to the issue of the Bonds in the form as stipulated\nL268@P8: in the Subscription Agreement;\nL269@P8: (d) the Bonds having been completed, executed and delivered as appropriate by the\nL270@P8: Company in accordance with the terms of the Subscription Agreement, the Trust Deed\nL271@P8: and the Agency Agreement substantially in the respective forms agreed between the\nL272@P8-9: Company and the Managers;– 10 –\nL273@P9: (e) the Managers having received the substantially complete drafts of the CSRC Filings and\nL274@P9: the opinion by the PRC counsel of the Company in relation to the CSRC Filings, such\nL275@P9: drafts to be in form and substance reasonably satisfactory to the Managers;\nL276@P9: (f) in the opinion of the Managers, there having been no adverse change, nor any\nL277@P9: development or event which involves, or is reasonably likely to involve, an adverse\nL278@P9: change in the earnings, net assets, business, operations, condition (financial or\nL279@P9: otherwise), or prospects of the Company and/or its subsidiaries that is material in the\nL280@P9: context of the issue and offering of the Bonds or which is likely to prejudice materially\nL281@P9: the issue and offering of the Bonds or dealings in the Bonds on the secondary market;\nL282@P9: (g) the representations and warranties by the Company contained in the Subscription\nL283@P9: Agreement being true and accurate on each date on which they are deemed to be repeated\nL284@P9: with reference in each case to the facts and circumstances then subsisting in accordance\nL285@P9: with the Subscription Agreement;\nL286@P9: (h) the Managers having received confirmation that listing approval from the Stock\nL287@P9: Exchange for the Conversion Shares issuable upon conversion of the Bonds has been\nL288@P9: obtained;\nL289@P9: (i) the Bonds and the relevant currency being accepted for settlement by Euroclear Bank\nL290@P9: SA/NV and Clearstream Banking S.A.;\nL291@P9: (j) the Trust Deed and the Agency Agreement being executed on or before the Issue Date,\nL292@P9: each in a form satisfactory to Managers, by or on behalf of all parties thereto; and\nL293@P9: (k) the Company not being in breach of the Subscription Agreement.\nL294@P9: The Managers may, at their discretion and upon such terms as they think fit, waive compliance\nL295@P9: with the whole or any part of the conditions set out above (other than paragraphs (e) and (j)).\nL296@P9: Termination\nL297@P9: Notwithstanding anything contained in the Subscription Agreement, if at any time prior to the\nL298@P9: payment of the proceeds of the issue of the Bonds to the Company on the Issue Date,\nL299@P9: (a) there develops, occurs or comes into force:\nL300@P9: (i) any material adverse change, or any development reasonably likely to involve a\nL301@P9: material adverse change, in the condition, financial or otherwise, or in the earnings,\nL302@P9: assets, business, operations or prospects of the Company, or the Company and its\nL303@P9-10: subsidiaries taken as a whole; or– 11 –\nL304@P10: (ii) any event, or series of events beyond the control of the Managers (including,\nL305@P10: without limitation any outbreak or escalation of hostilities, act of terrorism, the\nL306@P10: declaration by Hong Kong, the PRC, Japan, Singapore, the United States, the\nL307@P10: United Kingdom, any member of the European Economic Area (“EEA”), or any\nL308@P10: jurisdiction where the Group has operations of a national emergency or war or\nL309@P10: other calamity or crisis); or\nL310@P10: (iii) any material adverse change or development involving a prospective material\nL311@P10: adverse change in or affecting the financial markets in Hong Kong, the PRC, Japan,\nL312@P10: Singapore, the United States, the United Kingdom, any member of the EEA, or any\nL313@P10: jurisdiction where the Group has operations or in international financial, political\nL314@P10: or economic conditions, currency exchange rates, exchange controls or taxation; or\nL315@P10: (iv) any material disruption in commercial banking or securities settlement or clearance\nL316@P10: services in Hong Kong, the PRC, Japan, Singapore, the United States, the United\nL317@P10: Kingdom or any member of the EEA and/or a general moratorium on commercial\nL318@P10: banking activities having been declared by the relevant authorities in Hong Kong,\nL319@P10: the PRC, Japan, Singapore, the United States, the United Kingdom, any member of\nL320@P10: the EEA or any jurisdiction where the Group has operations; or\nL321@P10: (v) any suspension of or limitation of trading (a) in any of the Company’s securities\nL322@P10: by the Stock Exchange (save and except for any trading halt in relation to the issue\nL323@P10: and offering of the Bonds) or any other exchange or over the counter market on\nL324@P10: which the Company’s securities are admitted or listed for trading, or (b) generally\nL325@P10: on the Stock Exchange, the Shanghai Stock Exchange, the Shenzhen Stock\nL326@P10: Exchange, the Tokyo Stock Exchange, the London Stock Exchange, the New York\nL327@P10: Stock Exchange or the Nasdaq National Market;\nL328@P10: that, in the sole judgment of the Managers, would make the offer and sale of the Bonds\nL329@P10: or the enforcement of contracts to purchase the Bonds impracticable or inadvisable, or\nL330@P10: would materially prejudice trading of the Bonds in the secondary market; and\nL331@P10: (b) if any of the conditions specified in the Subscription Agreement has not been satisfied or\nL332@P10: waived by the Managers on or prior to the Issue Date,\nL333@P10: then and in any such case, the Managers may terminate the Subscription Agreement without\nL334@P10: liability to the Company by giving notice orally or in writing to the Company, which notice\nL335@P10: may be given at any time prior to the payment of the proceeds of the issue of the Bonds to the\nL336@P10-11: Company on the Issue Date.– 12 –\nL337@P11: Lock-up Undertakings by the Company under the Subscription Agreement\nL338@P11: The Company has undertaken to the Managers in the Subscription Agreement that neither\nL339@P11: the Company nor any person acting on its or their behalf will (a) effect or arrange or procure\nL340@P11: placement of, allot or issue or offer to allot or issue or grant any option, right or warrant\nL341@P11: to subscribe for, or enter into any transaction which is designed to, or might reasonably\nL342@P11: be expected to, result in any of the aforesaid (whether by actual disposition or effective\nL343@P11: economic disposition due to cash settlement or otherwise), directly or indirectly, any equity\nL344@P11: securities of the Company or any securities convertible into, or exercisable, or exchangeable\nL345@P11: for, equity securities of the Company, or (b) enter into any swap or similar agreement that\nL346@P11: transfers, in whole or in part, the economic risk of ownership of such Shares, whether any\nL347@P11: such transaction described in (a) or (b) above is to be settled by delivery of Shares or such\nL348@P11: other securities, in cash or otherwise, or (c) publicly announce an intention to effect any such\nL349@P11: transaction, in any such case without the prior written consent of the Managers, between the\nL350@P11: date of the Subscription Agreement and the date which is 60 days after the Issue Date (both\nL351@P11: dates inclusive), except for (i) the Bonds and the Conversion Shares issued on conversion of\nL352@P11: the Bonds, (ii) the issuance of the Placing Shares and (iii) the allotment and issuance of any\nL353@P11: Shares or the grant of equity-based awards pursuant to the terms of 2026 share award scheme\nL354@P11: of the Company adopted on June 22, 2026 in compliance with the applicable requirements of\nL355@P11: the Listing Rules from time to time. For the purposes of this paragraph, “Shares” means (i)\nL356@P11: ordinary shares issued by the Company to investors which are traded in Hong Kong dollars\nL357@P11: on the Stock Exchange; (ii) ordinary shares issued by the Company to investors in the PRC\nL358@P11: and (iii) any other fully-paid and non-assessable shares of any class or classes of the ordinary\nL359@P11: shares of the Company authorised after the date of the Subscription Agreement which have\nL360@P11: no preference in respect of dividends or of amounts payable in the event of any voluntary or\nL361@P11-12: involuntary liquidation or dissolution of the Company.– 13 –\nL362@P12: Principal Terms of the Bonds\nL363@P12: The principal terms of the Bonds are summarized as follows:\nL364@P12: Issuer: The Company\n"
